# Reverse proxy + TLS termination for the dashboard.
#
# DOMAIN (set in .env) controls how Caddy gets a certificate:
#   - A real domain name, with its DNS A record pointed at this host's
#     public IP and ports 80+443 reachable from the internet: Caddy
#     automatically obtains and renews a real Let's Encrypt certificate.
#     No other config needed -- just set DOMAIN and restart caddy.
#   - Unset (defaults to "localhost" below): Caddy uses its own internal
#     CA to self-sign a certificate instead. Works immediately for local
#     testing, but browsers will show an untrusted-certificate warning
#     until you either trust that internal CA locally or switch to a real
#     DOMAIN.
{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	encode gzip zstd
	reverse_proxy api:8000
}
